1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,070
Characters, actions, places, occupations,
and events in this series

2
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:08,750
are fictional and created
for entertainment purposes only.

3
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:13,280
They are not intended to urge
or promote any behavior in the series.

4
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,720
Viewer discretion is advised.

5
00:00:16,190 --> 00:00:17,330
I’ll do everything to find Key.

6
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:18,800
Key.

7
00:00:19,590 --> 00:00:22,200
Thank you for saving me.

8
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:23,600
Key, honey.

9
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:26,380
I was the one
who made her condition worse.

10
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,120
It was my fault.

11
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:30,900
You’re the best dad to me.

12
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:33,970
Are we really going to sleep over here?

13
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:08,550
You can’t sleep?

14
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:14,900
Yes.

15
00:02:42,770 --> 00:02:43,800
Are you afraid?

16
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:53,600
I’m afraid that if I fall asleep,

17
00:02:56,770 --> 00:02:58,500
I will have a nightmare about my mom.

18
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,600
I don’t want to see it again.

19
00:03:10,270 --> 00:03:12,040
If you don’t want
to have the nightmare again,

20
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:15,580
why don’t we face it together?

21
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:32,800
Key.

22
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:43,600
It’s okay.

23
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:46,600
It’s alright.

24
00:06:56,740 --> 00:06:57,900
You are okay now.

25
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:03,290
Everything was just the past.

26
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:37,880
How are you feeling?

27
00:08:37,919 --> 00:08:39,400
Did you get a good sleep last night?

28
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:53,850
Mom.

29
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:57,770
I miss you.

30
00:08:58,650 --> 00:08:59,980
I’m right here.

31
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:03,960
Do you know…

32
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:06,720
how incredible you are?

33
00:09:09,330 --> 00:09:11,400
My daughter is the best.

34
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:16,370
I love you, Mom.

35
00:09:21,420 --> 00:09:22,800
I love you, too.

36
00:09:30,290 --> 00:09:31,900
So Key,

37
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,400
you don’t need to be sad,

38
00:09:35,460 --> 00:09:36,800
feel hurt,

39
00:09:37,620 --> 00:09:39,500
or feel guilty anymore.

40
00:09:44,130 --> 00:09:49,450
The love you gave me made me very happy.

41
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,900
Key, promise me.

42
00:09:59,850 --> 00:10:02,700
You will go on living a happy life.

43
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:04,780
Can you do that?

44
00:10:10,970 --> 00:10:12,100
I promise.

45
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,100
I will be happy.

46
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:49,600
You are smiling.

47
00:10:54,650 --> 00:10:56,000
Did you have a good dream?

48
00:10:59,990 --> 00:11:00,800
Yes.

49
00:11:02,350 --> 00:11:03,500
I had a good dream.

50
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,500
I dreamt of my mom.

51
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:17,700
I promised her that I would be happy.

52
00:11:19,830 --> 00:11:20,800
That’s great.

53
00:11:25,580 --> 00:11:27,300
You are my happiness.

54
00:12:35,450 --> 00:12:36,500
What did the doctor say?

55
00:12:37,930 --> 00:12:40,900
We talked a lot.

56
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:45,100
I haven’t seen a psychiatrist for a while.

57
00:12:46,250 --> 00:12:48,200
So I needed to update her
about my condition.

58
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:55,500
She said I made the right decision
to receive counselling again.

59
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:58,370
In the meantime,

60
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:01,000
I will receive counselling

61
00:13:02,710 --> 00:13:05,800
and take the prescribed medication.

62
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:11,150
Did she give you other recommendations?

63
00:13:12,020 --> 00:13:14,900
Is there anything that can help you heal?

64
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:21,700
She said that having someone I love,

65
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:24,150
someone who understands me by my side,

66
00:13:24,730 --> 00:13:26,200
would be a big help.

67
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:28,600
I already have them.

68
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:32,200
I have you and everyone in my family.

69
00:13:39,050 --> 00:13:41,680
Thank you, Chan,
for keeping me company today.

70
00:13:43,170 --> 00:13:44,100
Company?

71
00:13:45,310 --> 00:13:46,400
I’m your girlfriend.

72
00:13:49,990 --> 00:13:51,000
Okay.

73
00:13:51,810 --> 00:13:54,320
Thank you for being my girlfriend.

74
00:13:56,970 --> 00:14:01,000
I will be by your side
and stick to you every day.

75
00:14:02,190 --> 00:14:04,880
Then I will stick to you

76
00:14:05,460 --> 00:14:07,800
like I'm attached to you at the hip.

77
00:14:15,410 --> 00:14:17,980
Before we go home,
we should go shopping for Simba’s stuff.

78
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:20,480
Sure.

79
00:14:20,520 --> 00:14:21,700
What are you going to buy for him?

80
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:25,200
I don’t know.

81
00:14:25,610 --> 00:14:27,000
I just want to buy him something.

82
00:14:29,130 --> 00:14:31,400
Don’t you want to buy
anything for this one?

83
00:14:34,340 --> 00:14:35,300
For this one,

84
00:14:35,830 --> 00:14:37,730
I’ll take care of her
for the rest of my life.

85
00:14:41,770 --> 00:14:42,500
Come on.

86
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:43,900
Let’s go shopping.

87
00:14:44,950 --> 00:14:45,800
Yeah.

88
00:15:03,290 --> 00:15:04,630
Where are you going?

89
00:15:06,060 --> 00:15:07,240
I’m going to Paris.

90
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:08,610
I have a shooting there.

91
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:11,100
Didn’t you just come back from Milan?

92
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:12,330
Are you leaving again?

93
00:15:12,850 --> 00:15:16,200
When an opportunity comes my way,
I have to take it, right?

94
00:15:17,070 --> 00:15:18,400
How long will you be away?

95
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:21,500
Around two weeks.

96
00:15:21,770 --> 00:15:22,730
Two weeks?

97
00:15:23,050 --> 00:15:23,560
Yes.

98
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:25,600
Who am I gonna have to keep me company?

99
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:28,300
You still have Aunt Mam.

100
00:15:28,630 --> 00:15:31,340
That’s different. She can’t replace you.

101
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:37,000
It’s nothing personal, Mam.

102
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:39,300
Yes.

103
00:15:41,730 --> 00:15:46,450
If you feel lonely,
why don’t you find something to do?

104
00:15:47,190 --> 00:15:50,210
I’m sure you have many things
you want to do,

105
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:54,150
especially meddling in Chan’s life.

106
00:15:59,890 --> 00:16:03,200
How could I meddle in her life?

107
00:16:08,930 --> 00:16:09,950
Mom.

108
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:14,700
While I’m away,
can you please be nice to Chan?

109
00:16:14,960 --> 00:16:16,000
I’m asking you.

110
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:17,240
Please.

111
00:16:23,630 --> 00:16:25,880
I’ve got to leave now,
otherwise I will miss my flight.

112
00:16:26,590 --> 00:16:27,330
I’ll see you.

113
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,700
Have a safe flight.

114
00:16:32,870 --> 00:16:33,530
Yes.

115
00:16:33,740 --> 00:16:34,900
I won’t see you off.

116
00:16:37,270 --> 00:16:38,300
I’m leaving.

117
00:16:43,110 --> 00:16:44,600
Aunt Mam, please take care of my mom.

118
00:17:15,010 --> 00:17:16,800
Why do you want me to come with you?

119
00:17:17,210 --> 00:17:18,400
It’s so early.

120
00:17:19,470 --> 00:17:20,599
I want you to come with me.

121
00:17:23,859 --> 00:17:27,200
While waiting for you,
I don’t know what to do.

122
00:17:27,730 --> 00:17:29,850
I have plenty of time
before my band practice at 1 p.m.

123
00:17:32,390 --> 00:17:34,500
Just do what you always do
when you come to my office.

124
00:17:36,490 --> 00:17:37,700
You mean, sitting around?

125
00:17:40,370 --> 00:17:41,500
You stare at me.

126
00:17:44,040 --> 00:17:44,800
Oh.

127
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:48,300
Did you know that I was staring at you?

128
00:17:49,750 --> 00:17:51,100
It would be weird if I didn’t know.

129
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:53,200
You couldn’t stop staring at me.

130
00:17:56,060 --> 00:17:58,150
We've always stuck together lately.

131
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:03,400
Then you two should spend some time apart.

132
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:08,150
Mom.

133
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:11,500
Good morning, Madam.

134
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:18,210
Chan, you know what you need to do, right?

135
00:18:21,250 --> 00:18:23,400
There’s nothing
I need to worry about, right?

136
00:18:24,850 --> 00:18:25,700
Yes.

137
00:18:26,360 --> 00:18:27,700
Don’t worry, Mom.

138
00:18:45,630 --> 00:18:47,100
I’m sorry for my mom.

139
00:18:49,220 --> 00:18:50,300
It’s okay.

140
00:18:51,810 --> 00:18:53,680
I shouldn’t have told you to come with me.

141
00:18:56,380 --> 00:18:59,200
You asked me to come with you
because you were worried about me.

142
00:18:59,750 --> 00:19:00,650
I know that.

143
00:19:04,480 --> 00:19:08,300
About your mom,

144
00:19:10,160 --> 00:19:13,800
she is the real last boss, like Sun said.

145
00:19:18,810 --> 00:19:22,700
But I believe that you can win her over.

146
00:19:30,090 --> 00:19:31,000
Let’s go.

147
00:19:49,580 --> 00:19:50,650
I thought

148
00:19:52,150 --> 00:19:53,970
you weren’t this kind of person.

149
00:20:03,790 --> 00:20:05,450
Do you have something to say to me?

150
00:20:12,740 --> 00:20:15,300
You’re not someone who gives up easily.

151
00:20:18,730 --> 00:20:20,800
The girl who is standing in front of me

152
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:24,550
is not Jay that I knew.

153
00:20:25,670 --> 00:20:27,480
You are not fighting alone.

154
00:20:29,190 --> 00:20:30,950
We have the same enemy.

155
00:20:39,380 --> 00:20:40,780
So Jay,

156
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:45,100
don’t give up yet.

157
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:37,740
Simba.

158
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:39,700
Mommy and Mama are back.

159
00:21:44,130 --> 00:21:45,700
Are you going to sleep over here?

160
00:21:47,750 --> 00:21:50,030
Your sister went abroad for work.

161
00:21:50,900 --> 00:21:51,800
I feel lonely.

162
00:21:52,180 --> 00:21:53,800
So I want to spend time with you.

163
00:21:57,490 --> 00:21:59,000
How long are you going to stay?

164
00:22:01,110 --> 00:22:02,090
Indefinitely.

165
00:22:06,090 --> 00:22:06,930
Whose cat is this?

166
00:22:10,150 --> 00:22:11,570
That’s my cat, Mom.

167
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:17,210
I never permitted you to call me Mom.

168
00:22:24,090 --> 00:22:25,600
I call you Mom

169
00:22:26,690 --> 00:22:29,100
because you are Chan’s Mom.

170
00:22:29,870 --> 00:22:31,180
I want to show you respect.

171
00:22:33,840 --> 00:22:35,200
You are good at talking back.

172
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:36,290
Mom.

173
00:22:36,840 --> 00:22:40,500
If you are going to stay with me,
please don’t pick a fight.

174
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:41,400
Why?

175
00:22:42,250 --> 00:22:43,730
Are you going to tell me to leave again?

176
00:22:48,170 --> 00:22:49,800
I’ll call you Madam.

177
00:22:51,190 --> 00:22:55,900
I’ll wait until you are comfortable
letting me call you Mom.

178
00:22:59,410 --> 00:23:00,600
It’s unlikely to happen.

179
00:23:04,720 --> 00:23:05,930
Put the cat somewhere else.

180
00:23:07,330 --> 00:23:08,360
I’m allergic to cats.

181
00:23:09,850 --> 00:23:11,030
You’ve never had an allergy.

182
00:23:11,070 --> 00:23:12,070
Yes, I do.

183
00:23:13,270 --> 00:23:14,880
I’m allergic to all kinds of animal fur.

184
00:23:22,940 --> 00:23:23,980
I got it.

185
00:23:24,700 --> 00:23:29,500
I’ll keep Simba in the bedroom only.

186
00:23:33,010 --> 00:23:33,800
Simba.

187
00:23:35,270 --> 00:23:36,200
Let's go.

188
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:48,300
I told you to take the cat somewhere else,

189
00:23:49,180 --> 00:23:50,880
not to keep it in your bedroom.

190
00:23:53,070 --> 00:23:54,490
Where do you want me to take him?

191
00:23:54,530 --> 00:23:56,500
Anywhere but here.

192
00:23:57,250 --> 00:23:59,250
I told you I’m allergic to animal fur.

193
00:23:59,390 --> 00:24:01,180
I’m keeping him only in my room.

194
00:24:01,220 --> 00:24:02,380
That’s not enough.

195
00:24:04,330 --> 00:24:05,270
Mom.

196
00:24:06,100 --> 00:24:07,500
Don’t you feel bad for him?

197
00:24:11,530 --> 00:24:12,500
Fine.

198
00:24:13,250 --> 00:24:15,400
Don’t let it come near me.

199
00:24:16,310 --> 00:24:17,800
I don’t want to see it.

200
00:24:23,810 --> 00:24:25,130
Good night, Mom.

201
00:24:26,380 --> 00:24:27,500
Good night.

202
00:24:52,030 --> 00:24:52,780
Chan.

203
00:24:54,030 --> 00:24:55,800
I’m not feeling well.

204
00:24:56,290 --> 00:24:57,530
I think I’m going to be sick.

205
00:24:58,010 --> 00:24:59,100
You are sick?

206
00:24:59,980 --> 00:25:02,030
I’ll call Aunt Mam
to come and take care of you.

207
00:25:02,070 --> 00:25:03,650
No, it will take too long.

208
00:25:05,250 --> 00:25:07,610
I want someone
to take care of me right now.

209
00:25:07,800 --> 00:25:10,330
Mom, I have to go to work.

210
00:25:10,490 --> 00:25:11,500
I know that.

211
00:25:13,280 --> 00:25:16,600
But she doesn’t have to go with you.

212
00:25:24,040 --> 00:25:25,650
You want me to stay and take care of you?

213
00:25:27,980 --> 00:25:29,770
If you have nothing else to do.

214
00:25:32,210 --> 00:25:33,720
I only have a schedule this evening.

215
00:25:34,070 --> 00:25:35,300
I have to perform with my band.

216
00:25:37,470 --> 00:25:38,250
Okay.

217
00:25:39,010 --> 00:25:41,970
I’ll have Eggs Benedict, avocado salad,

218
00:25:42,140 --> 00:25:44,900
Kyoho grapes, and mineral water
for breakfast.

219
00:25:45,740 --> 00:25:50,300
For lunch, I want to eat Spanish food.

220
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:52,130
Do you know how to make paella?

221
00:25:55,560 --> 00:25:56,600
Mom.

222
00:25:57,150 --> 00:25:58,570
You can order it from a restaurant.

223
00:25:58,890 --> 00:25:59,980
Why?

224
00:26:00,470 --> 00:26:02,200
Can’t you prepare them for me?

225
00:26:04,150 --> 00:26:05,210
Of course, I can.

226
00:26:06,310 --> 00:26:07,500
No problem.

227
00:26:08,050 --> 00:26:09,100
Mom.

228
00:26:10,630 --> 00:26:12,300
Oops, I mean, Madam.

229
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:32,380
I don’t want to leave you alone with Mom.

230
00:26:35,720 --> 00:26:36,800
It’s okay.

231
00:26:37,590 --> 00:26:38,700
Don’t worry about me.

232
00:26:40,950 --> 00:26:44,200
I think my mom must be up to something.

233
00:26:46,150 --> 00:26:47,200
I know.

234
00:26:48,050 --> 00:26:49,550
I also have something up my sleeve.

235
00:26:51,410 --> 00:26:52,400
What is it?

236
00:26:55,020 --> 00:26:56,100
I can’t tell you.

237
00:26:58,970 --> 00:27:00,600
Will you two end up fighting again?

238
00:27:01,870 --> 00:27:04,530
I think I should take leave today.

239
00:27:05,490 --> 00:27:06,500
Don’t do that.

240
00:27:07,040 --> 00:27:09,140
Even if you took leave,
your mom wouldn’t leave me alone.

241
00:27:09,870 --> 00:27:14,370
It would give her a chance
to criticize you.

242
00:27:16,500 --> 00:27:17,900
I’m worried about you.

243
00:27:22,940 --> 00:27:24,000
You should go to work.

244
00:27:31,090 --> 00:27:31,900
Fine.

245
00:27:36,560 --> 00:27:37,400
Bye.

246
00:28:23,670 --> 00:28:24,600
What’s up, Phu?

247
00:28:29,530 --> 00:28:32,210
Every time you have that look on your face
when you come to see me,

248
00:28:33,470 --> 00:28:34,600
it’s always about Jay.

249
00:28:37,700 --> 00:28:38,900
You’re right.

250
00:28:41,510 --> 00:28:43,050
I told you.

251
00:28:43,640 --> 00:28:46,400
If it’s about Jay,
I don’t want to hear it.

252
00:28:55,740 --> 00:28:57,500
Can you hear me out this time?

253
00:29:00,900 --> 00:29:02,700
I won’t bother you about this again.

254
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:08,600
I came to tell you about Jay

255
00:29:10,590 --> 00:29:11,920
because I feel bad for her.

256
00:29:13,740 --> 00:29:15,570
I’ve never seen her in such a wreck.

257
00:29:16,900 --> 00:29:18,400
She is a complete mess.

258
00:29:20,390 --> 00:29:21,300
I think,

259
00:29:22,790 --> 00:29:24,670
for the sake of our long friendship,

260
00:29:26,380 --> 00:29:27,750
can you go talk to her?

261
00:29:29,540 --> 00:29:31,410
So you won’t have anything unresolved
between you two.

262
00:29:35,090 --> 00:29:37,100
Jay wants to talk to you one last time.

263
00:30:34,520 --> 00:30:36,850
I’m glad that you came to see me.

264
00:30:41,130 --> 00:30:43,800
Phu told me you wanted to talk to me.

265
00:30:45,430 --> 00:30:46,300
What is it?

266
00:30:54,280 --> 00:30:55,500
If…

267
00:31:00,890 --> 00:31:02,770
I hadn’t left you back then,

268
00:31:05,540 --> 00:31:10,300
what do you think we’d be like now?

269
00:31:13,370 --> 00:31:17,630
Would we still love each other?

270
00:31:18,810 --> 00:31:23,300
Would we get married
and have our happy ending?

271
00:31:29,090 --> 00:31:30,400
Please say something.

272
00:31:46,130 --> 00:31:47,600
Our relationship,

273
00:31:51,380 --> 00:31:52,700
it’s too late.

274
00:31:54,820 --> 00:31:56,000
The thing that you said,

275
00:31:58,490 --> 00:31:59,980
it will never happen.

276
00:32:01,490 --> 00:32:02,700
You and I,

277
00:32:03,580 --> 00:32:05,100
we are not in love anymore.

278
00:32:11,680 --> 00:32:13,300
Everything about us is just the past.

279
00:32:15,880 --> 00:32:17,500
I want you to move on.

280
00:32:25,380 --> 00:32:26,700
You need to focus on the present.

281
00:32:29,820 --> 00:32:32,200
But I want to have you in my present.

282
00:32:36,640 --> 00:32:37,760
No, Jay.

283
00:32:38,060 --> 00:32:41,400
You and I can only be friends.

284
00:32:43,260 --> 00:32:45,300
But I don’t want to be your friend.

285
00:32:58,840 --> 00:33:01,180
This is the last time that we talk.

286
00:33:08,210 --> 00:33:09,200
You know what?

287
00:33:14,060 --> 00:33:16,700
I never thought I could be such a loser.

288
00:33:26,590 --> 00:33:28,500
Then go back to being the old you.

289
00:33:51,120 --> 00:33:53,700
Can you give me another chance?

290
00:34:00,260 --> 00:34:02,550
You’re asking for something
I can’t give you.

291
00:34:06,320 --> 00:34:07,600
I really love Key.

292
00:34:23,540 --> 00:34:25,000
Are you sure?

293
00:34:35,030 --> 00:34:35,900
Jay.

294
00:34:37,179 --> 00:34:41,500
I think our love is
better left as a memory.

295
00:34:45,639 --> 00:34:46,900
I want you…

296
00:34:48,920 --> 00:34:51,199
to remember only
the good memories about us.

297
00:34:56,150 --> 00:34:58,700
Even though our love has ended,

298
00:35:02,240 --> 00:35:03,840
I don’t want it to be ruined.

299
00:35:09,610 --> 00:35:11,100
I can put myself back together.

300
00:35:12,610 --> 00:35:14,000
So can you.

301
00:35:17,160 --> 00:35:20,660
Jay that I knew, she can definitely do it.

302
00:35:56,480 --> 00:35:58,100
Be careful.

303
00:36:05,200 --> 00:36:06,300
Your mom…

304
00:36:09,310 --> 00:36:11,200
will never accept Key.

305
00:36:17,260 --> 00:36:18,300
Thank you.

306
00:37:27,530 --> 00:37:28,760
Why did you stop walking?

307
00:37:29,980 --> 00:37:31,120
Did I forget something?

308
00:37:34,220 --> 00:37:35,200
Forgot what?

309
00:37:36,210 --> 00:37:38,000
I’m asking you.

310
00:37:42,960 --> 00:37:44,250
Did you forget your bag?

311
00:37:44,580 --> 00:37:46,900
Where did you leave it?

312
00:37:47,610 --> 00:37:49,070
Where do you think I left it?

313
00:37:52,340 --> 00:37:53,330
In the car?

314
00:37:53,640 --> 00:37:55,180
Then go check it.

315
00:37:57,640 --> 00:38:01,290
I’ll put these bags in the room first.
Then I’ll go down to check it.

316
00:38:01,540 --> 00:38:02,380
No.

317
00:38:04,160 --> 00:38:05,170
You need to go check it right now.

318
00:38:06,860 --> 00:38:08,730
Can you take these bags to the room?

319
00:38:09,330 --> 00:38:10,200
No.

320
00:38:11,030 --> 00:38:12,800
I’m tired. I’ll go wait in the room.

321
00:38:15,540 --> 00:38:17,700
Why don’t you take these bags with you?

322
00:38:18,570 --> 00:38:19,890
I’ll go check your bag in the car.

323
00:38:20,490 --> 00:38:21,370
Please.

324
00:38:25,300 --> 00:38:26,100
No.

325
00:38:55,020 --> 00:38:56,400
Why did it take you so long?

326
00:38:56,440 --> 00:38:57,900
I almost don’t want to wait anymore.

327
00:38:59,550 --> 00:39:00,800
I’m sorry to keep you waiting.

328
00:39:06,730 --> 00:39:08,600
It looks similar to the original recipe.

329
00:39:10,180 --> 00:39:10,900
Yes.

330
00:39:11,600 --> 00:39:14,290
I cooked it for my family before.

331
00:39:15,690 --> 00:39:16,550
Really?

332
00:39:17,850 --> 00:39:19,170
Did they eat it?

333
00:39:20,340 --> 00:39:22,000
They said it was delicious.

334
00:39:22,630 --> 00:39:24,300
I learned it from a talented chef.

335
00:39:27,310 --> 00:39:29,360
Did you hire a chef
from Spain to teach you?

336
00:39:30,650 --> 00:39:31,500
No.

337
00:39:31,780 --> 00:39:32,900
I learned from Chef Niam,

338
00:39:33,550 --> 00:39:35,330
a house helper who works for my family.

339
00:39:35,370 --> 00:39:36,700
She is an amazing cook.

340
00:39:37,150 --> 00:39:38,800
She learned the recipe from YouTube.

341
00:39:43,110 --> 00:39:45,400
If it doesn’t taste good, I won’t eat it.

342
00:39:46,890 --> 00:39:48,490
Yes, me too.

343
00:40:11,710 --> 00:40:12,600
How is it?

344
00:40:13,930 --> 00:40:16,400
Does it suit your palate, Mom?

345
00:40:18,890 --> 00:40:20,500
I mean, Madam.

346
00:40:42,750 --> 00:40:45,130
May I be excused to check on Simba?

347
00:41:32,230 --> 00:41:33,400
What are you doing?

348
00:41:34,740 --> 00:41:36,370
Why don’t you read my message?

349
00:41:49,420 --> 00:41:50,570
What are they doing?

350
00:42:15,470 --> 00:42:17,800
Mom, you seem to enjoy your meal.

351
00:42:20,440 --> 00:42:21,800
Where is Key?

352
00:42:23,550 --> 00:42:25,200
You smell so good.

353
00:42:31,920 --> 00:42:33,190
(What are you doing, hooman?)

354
00:42:36,410 --> 00:42:37,450
Key.

355
00:42:41,370 --> 00:42:42,700
I’m watching our cat.

356
00:42:44,110 --> 00:42:45,200
Meow.

357
00:42:45,870 --> 00:42:46,970
Meow, meow.

358
00:42:47,690 --> 00:42:49,700
(Do your best at work, hooman.)

359
00:42:54,160 --> 00:42:56,640
This cat is quite something.

360
00:42:57,580 --> 00:42:58,800
(Good luck with work.)

361
00:43:00,020 --> 00:43:00,900
(Meow.)

362
00:43:45,160 --> 00:43:45,900
Shit.

363
00:43:46,290 --> 00:43:47,300
Again?

364
00:43:48,490 --> 00:43:49,300
Yes.

365
00:43:49,810 --> 00:43:50,950
You got drunk again.

366
00:44:01,660 --> 00:44:03,600
You are wearing my pajamas.

367
00:44:04,130 --> 00:44:05,630
Please wash before returning.

368
00:44:11,060 --> 00:44:12,300
What happened last night?

369
00:44:15,450 --> 00:44:16,490
Do you really want to know?

370
00:44:24,860 --> 00:44:26,280
Don’t you remember…

371
00:44:28,610 --> 00:44:30,100
what we did?

372
00:44:49,860 --> 00:44:50,600
Elle.

373
00:44:53,040 --> 00:44:53,840
Hi, Phu.

374
00:45:00,360 --> 00:45:01,800
Did you follow me?

375
00:45:03,350 --> 00:45:04,400
Calm down, Jay.

376
00:45:05,290 --> 00:45:06,600
I invited her.

377
00:45:08,780 --> 00:45:10,000
Why didn’t you tell me sooner?

378
00:45:12,080 --> 00:45:13,250
So I would go to another bar.

379
00:45:13,890 --> 00:45:15,100
Wait.

380
00:45:16,020 --> 00:45:17,600
Why do you keep running away from me?

381
00:45:21,570 --> 00:45:22,500
No, I don’t.

382
00:45:24,170 --> 00:45:25,400
Are you…

383
00:45:26,430 --> 00:45:27,300
having feelings for me?

384
00:45:35,610 --> 00:45:36,800
No way.

385
00:45:37,890 --> 00:45:39,400
Then let’s have a drink together.

386
00:45:41,540 --> 00:45:42,570
Are you asking me out on a date?

387
00:45:44,010 --> 00:45:44,840
Yes.

388
00:45:46,300 --> 00:45:48,320
It’s a friend date.

389
00:45:50,380 --> 00:45:51,600
Nothing romantic.

390
00:45:52,980 --> 00:45:54,600
Nothing…

391
00:45:55,810 --> 00:45:56,700
sexual.

392
00:46:02,280 --> 00:46:04,150
Can I have a strong Vodka?

393
00:46:10,440 --> 00:46:11,400
Do you dare?

394
00:46:15,440 --> 00:46:16,700
I thought you would dare.

395
00:46:34,860 --> 00:46:36,850
You live up to your reputation,
Miss Boozer.

396
00:46:39,520 --> 00:46:40,780
Can I have another glass?

397
00:47:23,830 --> 00:47:25,030
I don’t get it.

398
00:47:26,020 --> 00:47:27,580
What is so special about that girl?

399
00:47:27,810 --> 00:47:29,600
Why is Chan so devoted to her?

400
00:47:31,450 --> 00:47:33,000
It’s no longer your business.

401
00:47:34,690 --> 00:47:36,120
Why are you worried about Chan?

402
00:47:38,240 --> 00:47:40,500
How can I not be worried about her?

403
00:47:41,050 --> 00:47:42,560
Look at what she’s doing.

404
00:47:44,610 --> 00:47:47,100
But she doesn’t want you to fuss over her.

405
00:47:48,740 --> 00:47:51,000
What Chat does is no longer your business.

406
00:47:55,300 --> 00:47:57,400
The only thing that you can do right now…

407
00:48:05,890 --> 00:48:06,850
is have a drink.

408
00:48:40,550 --> 00:48:43,000
I secretly did some digging on you.

409
00:48:47,250 --> 00:48:51,800
You are a well-known pilot.

410
00:48:53,250 --> 00:48:56,240
You are the most talented female pilot
in your class.

411
00:49:00,750 --> 00:49:03,400
You like secretly
dating flight attendants.

412
00:49:06,290 --> 00:49:08,630
Who knows how many airlines
you’ve dated by now?

413
00:49:27,820 --> 00:49:29,750
I’m not a flight attendant.

414
00:49:33,920 --> 00:49:36,700
But are you interested in
keeping me company tonight?

415
00:49:55,650 --> 00:50:00,930
So you and I,

416
00:50:04,590 --> 00:50:05,920
did we sleep together?

417
00:50:16,800 --> 00:50:17,700
No way.

418
00:50:18,750 --> 00:50:20,270
Why don’t I remember anything?

419
00:50:20,310 --> 00:50:22,090
I remember that we were in a nightclub.

420
00:50:22,430 --> 00:50:24,200
Then I blacked out.

421
00:50:28,690 --> 00:50:29,780
Why are you laughing?

422
00:50:31,280 --> 00:50:32,200
Listen.

423
00:50:33,040 --> 00:50:35,000
Since the day you first met me,

424
00:50:35,630 --> 00:50:37,800
the closest that we got was

425
00:50:41,600 --> 00:50:44,120
when you rolled over to hold me
before you woke up.

426
00:50:45,160 --> 00:50:47,040
Nothing happened between us.

427
00:50:47,080 --> 00:50:49,100
Because I rejected you.

428
00:50:50,070 --> 00:50:51,770
After that, you got wasted

429
00:50:51,880 --> 00:50:53,940
and threw up
on the side of the road again.

430
00:50:54,290 --> 00:50:56,300
So I needed to take you back to my room.

431
00:50:56,950 --> 00:50:58,600
I changed your clothes.

432
00:51:00,110 --> 00:51:02,370
Then I put you into the bed
because I felt sorry for you.

433
00:51:02,640 --> 00:51:03,540
Do you get it now?

434
00:51:03,580 --> 00:51:04,370
That’s not true.

435
00:51:04,480 --> 00:51:07,130
Sorry, but it’s true, darling.

436
00:51:07,950 --> 00:51:10,430
You should go take a shower.
Then I’ll give you a ride home.

437
00:51:12,860 --> 00:51:14,160
Why will you give me a ride home?

438
00:51:14,700 --> 00:51:16,780
When you get drunk next time,

439
00:51:17,210 --> 00:51:19,000
I’ll know where to drop you off.

440
00:51:19,890 --> 00:51:23,100
So you won’t have
to sleep over here, honey.

441
00:51:27,490 --> 00:51:28,900
Or do you want me
to help you take a shower?

442
00:51:28,940 --> 00:51:29,800
Come here.

443
00:51:30,870 --> 00:51:33,590
-You weren’t resisting last night.
-No.

444
00:52:04,610 --> 00:52:06,100
Aren’t you going to say thank you?

445
00:52:13,740 --> 00:52:15,100
Thank you for giving me a ride.

446
00:52:19,310 --> 00:52:21,100
Do you want to get
a cup of coffee tomorrow?

447
00:52:22,930 --> 00:52:24,330
Are you asking me out on a date?

448
00:52:28,950 --> 00:52:30,400
It’s just friends hanging out.

449
00:52:31,800 --> 00:52:32,700
No?

450
00:52:34,490 --> 00:52:36,800
Are you having feelings for me?

451
00:52:39,080 --> 00:52:39,820
Is that a joke?

452
00:52:39,860 --> 00:52:41,080
I have no feelings for you.

453
00:52:42,350 --> 00:52:43,180
So?

454
00:52:43,940 --> 00:52:45,020
Are you going?

455
00:52:46,110 --> 00:52:47,730
If you say no, I’ll go ask someone else.

456
00:52:52,150 --> 00:52:53,640
My answer is no.

457
00:52:53,930 --> 00:52:55,180
Do whatever you want.

458
00:52:56,370 --> 00:52:58,100
Okay. I got it.

459
00:52:58,830 --> 00:53:00,800
Have a nice day, Miss Jay.

460
00:53:06,100 --> 00:53:08,000
That’s it?
Aren’t you going to try a little harder?

461
00:53:15,560 --> 00:53:16,670
What the f*ck!

462
00:53:59,050 --> 00:54:00,600
Don’t drag this out.

463
00:54:00,940 --> 00:54:02,400
You’ll only end up hurting more.

464
00:54:04,400 --> 00:54:05,500
I agree.

465
00:54:05,970 --> 00:54:09,600
You should come to terms
with Chan’s decision.

466
00:54:10,260 --> 00:54:14,800
No matter what,
I will never break up with Chan.

467
00:54:18,960 --> 00:54:20,000
Can I ask you something?

468
00:54:21,130 --> 00:54:23,300
Do you really think
Chan will choose you over me?

469
00:54:26,440 --> 00:54:28,500
She doesn’t need to choose.

470
00:54:30,120 --> 00:54:31,800
She can have us both.

471
00:54:33,400 --> 00:54:34,300
Is that so?

472
00:54:35,750 --> 00:54:38,370
We are only going to take
our hatred out on each other.

473
00:54:39,830 --> 00:54:41,100
It will be very toxic.

474
00:54:41,830 --> 00:54:43,270
Don’t you feel sorry for Chan?

475
00:54:46,750 --> 00:54:49,050
Why do we have to hate each other?

476
00:54:54,330 --> 00:54:55,170
No way.

477
00:55:20,240 --> 00:55:21,200
Mom.

478
00:55:27,250 --> 00:55:28,570
I love you.

479
00:55:32,920 --> 00:55:34,780
I invited you to join me today.

480
00:55:37,520 --> 00:55:39,300
Because I want you to be present

481
00:55:41,640 --> 00:55:44,100
in the most important moment of my life.

482
00:56:45,390 --> 00:56:47,400
I will use these earrings

483
00:56:50,770 --> 00:56:52,400
to propose to you.

484
00:57:00,680 --> 00:57:02,200
Will you marry me, Key?

485
00:57:42,020 --> 00:57:45,100
Your mom will never accept me.

486
00:57:45,560 --> 00:57:46,730
Don’t give up yet.

487
00:57:47,180 --> 00:57:48,250
Don’t leave me.

488
00:57:48,660 --> 00:57:50,570
I will never give up on us.

489
00:57:51,630 --> 00:57:53,500
I want you to stop holding on to it.

490
00:57:53,820 --> 00:57:55,520
If you keep doing this,

491
00:57:55,800 --> 00:57:57,700
you may end up losing Chan as a friend.

492
00:57:58,540 --> 00:57:59,300
Simba.

493
00:58:00,010 --> 00:58:01,880
I don’t know where Mom took Simba.

494
00:58:02,210 --> 00:58:04,280
I checked the camera.
I didn’t see anyone home.

495
00:58:04,510 --> 00:58:09,330
I’m afraid that Mom
is willing to do anything to win.

496
00:58:10,900 --> 00:58:12,240
Honey.

497
00:58:12,280 --> 00:58:13,570
What do you want to talk to me about?

498
00:58:14,020 --> 00:58:15,570
Key is the only one I will marry.

499
00:58:15,840 --> 00:58:18,210
If you want me to accept your marriage,

500
00:58:18,660 --> 00:58:20,530
then you need to give me
something in exchange.
